{"id": "F1-str-format-attribute", "failure_class": "F1", "source_lib": "Jinja2", "provenance": "CVE-2016-10516 / Ronacher, 'Be Careful with Python's New-Style String Format'", "expression": "\"{0.__class__}\".format(x)", "stage": "validate", "context": "data", "expect_message": "method calls on values", "note": "The canonical F1 climb. format() performs getattr at runtime from the format string, which no static AST check reads."}
{"id": "F1-str-format-map", "failure_class": "F1", "source_lib": "Jinja2", "provenance": "CVE-2019-10906", "expression": "\"{0.__class__}\".format_map(x)", "stage": "validate", "context": "data", "expect_message": "method calls on values", "note": "format_map was the 2019 bypass of the 2016 format() fix."}
{"id": "F1-restrictedpython-format", "failure_class": "F1", "source_lib": "RestrictedPython", "provenance": "CVE-2023-41039", "expression": "\"{x.__class__}\".format(x=x)", "stage": "validate", "context": "data", "expect_message": "method calls on values", "note": "The keyword argument is also rejected, but the method call is the earlier problem in the source and so the one reported. Two independent barriers."}
