{"id": "F1-percent-mapping-key", "failure_class": "F1", "source_lib": "safeexpr", "provenance": "found while writing this corpus, 2026-08-23", "expression": "\"%(__class__)s\" % d", "stage": "evaluate", "context": "data", "expect_message": "string formatting", "note": "FOUND HERE. %-formatting does its own __getitem__ in C, so it bypassed the underscore-key block entirely. The design bans % from the registry, but % is an operator, so that ban never applied."}
{"id": "F1-percent-repr-leak", "failure_class": "F1", "source_lib": "safeexpr", "provenance": "found while writing this corpus, 2026-08-23", "expression": "\"%r\" % obj", "stage": "evaluate", "context": "object", "expect_message": "string formatting", "note": "FOUND HERE. %r handed a context object's full repr to the expression author as a value, the exact leak R8 keeps out of error messages."}
{"id": "F1-percent-str-leak", "failure_class": "F1", "source_lib": "safeexpr", "provenance": "found while writing this corpus, 2026-08-23", "expression": "\"%s\" % obj", "stage": "evaluate", "context": "object", "expect_message": "string formatting"}
{"id": "F1-fstring", "failure_class": "F1", "source_lib": "asteval", "provenance": "CVE-2025-24359 (same class, f-string spelling)", "expression": "f\"{x}\"", "stage": "validate", "context": "data", "expect_message": "f-strings"}
